# CloudNova Revenue Intelligence — example environment file
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO KEY IS NEEDED TO RUN THIS PROJECT.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The default path needs no API key, no account and no network access:
#
#     pip install duckdb pyyaml
#     python -m app
#     python -m app --ask "What was our total recognized revenue in USD for paid invoices in 2024?"
#
# DuckDB runs inside the Python process and reads the CSV directly, and the
# --ask layer answers by matching your question to one of a fixed set of known
# questions and running a reviewed SQL query against the gold tables. That
# matching is local string and keyword work. Nothing leaves the machine.
#
# You only need this file at all if you choose to enable the OPTIONAL general
# text-to-SQL path described below. To do that, copy this file to `.env` and
# fill in the key. `.env` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: general text-to-SQL path (OFF by default)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment and set this ONLY if you want to enable the optional path that sends
# an unrecognised question to a language model to generate SQL, instead of
# declining it.
#
# It is off by default on purpose. A deterministic answer to a revenue question
# is auditable and free; a generated one needs its own evaluation set and a
# published accuracy figure before anyone should rely on it. See the README,
# "What I deliberately left", item 1.
#
# Enabling this path means questions are sent to a third-party API over the
# network. The default path does neither.
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
